      "slug": "20260624-094244-high-emissivity-technology-emissivity-is",
      "issue_number": "12",
      "client": "NOVOTA",
      "topic": "High Emissivity Technology Emissivity is a measure of a material's ability to emit energy as thermal radiation. It refers to the ability of a material to emit or absorb thermal radiation compared to a perfect black body, which is an idealized object that absorbs all radiation that falls on it.  High emissivity technology is an one-of-a-kind approach to improve the thermal management of materials and surfaces by making an object behave more like a black body in terms of its thermal radiation properties. In essence, high-emissivity coatings maximize the ability of the surface to emit thermal radiation.  High emissivity technology is a crucial aspect of many of our heat management coatings and paints, including heat reflective coating, heat dissipation coating, and heat conservation coating.  Benefits 01 Improves energy efficiency 02 Enhanced thermal performance 03 Versatility",
